    fix: pin the codex smoke turn's provider and model on argv — the cell measured a dead router. Addresses CF-227.
    
    tests/harness-conformance.sh ran
    
        codex exec --skip-git-repo-check -s workspace-write "$prompt"
    
    with NEITHER a provider NOR a model, so the turn inherited `model_provider =
    "claude-code-router"`, `model = "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"` and `base_url =
    "http://127.0.0.1:3456/v1"` from this host's `~/.codex/config.toml`. Nothing listens
    on that port and no claude-code-router process exists: every smoke turn died with
    `ERROR: Reconnecting... waiting for network` (five retries, exit 124, no artifact), and
    that FAIL was the `codex:smoke` cell in docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md. The release gate
    for the word "supported" was measuring a router this repo never installed, not the
    harness it did install.
    
    What changed:
    
    - the codex arm of smoke_turn() pins both halves of the binding on argv:
      `-c "model_provider=\"$CODEX_PROVIDER\"" -m "$CODEX_MODEL" -- "$prompt"`, with
      CODEX_PROVIDER=openai (specs/HARNESS-MATRIX.md §3: codex hosts OpenAI natively) and
      HC_CODEX_MODEL (default gpt-6-luna) documented in the script header next to
      HC_TIMEOUT/HC_APPLY_TIMEOUT, and echoed into the generated doc's command line;
    - the credential is still the host's own `~/.codex/auth.json`, already named by
      cred_codex — no code path copies, moves or rewrites that file, and a genuinely absent
      credential is still a SKIP naming it (tests/selftest.sh §45 arm (a) keeps that red);
    - the PASS row names the pinned provider, the pinned model, the artifact's byte count and
      its sha256, so the cell says which provider was measured; a failing turn names the
      provider, the model and the base_url attempted (read from the pinned provider, or the
      URL codex itself reported) instead of only quoting "waiting for network";
    - exit 0 is not evidence: a turn that exits 0 without the artifact is a FAIL reading
      exactly `exited 0 without writing smoke.txt`, and wrong bytes are a FAIL reading
      `wrote smoke.txt without the token`. Measured trap: with an isolated CODEX_HOME a turn
      logged `failed to spawn code-mode host ~/.local/codex/0.166.0/bin/codex-code-mode-host:
      No such file or directory` and still exited 0 with no file;
    - specs/HARNESS-MATRIX.md §2's codex row no longer claims "not installed here | adapter in
      crier ... no binary, no installer", which contradicted specs/HARNESS.md (MEASURED
      install, scripts/harness/install-codex.sh, pin 0.166.0, exec surface). Specs are the
      design authority (AGENTS.md r1), so the stale row was corrected rather than the claim
      removed; it also records that the smoke turn pins the provider because an ambient
      config may name a router;
    - tests/selftest.sh §45 gets one new fixture arm (no network, no credential value, no
      model token): a PATH `codex` stub records its own argv and writes no artifact, so the
      arm proves `-c model_provider="openai"`, `-m fixture-codex-model` (the HC_CODEX_MODEL
      knob) and the smoke needle reach the argv, that a stub exiting 0 with no artifact is
      refused by that exact name, and — the control — that the pre-CF-227 arm spliced back
      into a scratch copy records an argv WITHOUT the pin, which is what makes the arm
      falsifiable.
    
    docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md was regenerated with `tests/harness-conformance.sh
    --write-doc` after codex:smoke read PASS; it is not hand-edited. The regeneration adds no
    new absolute host paths — the generator renders $HOME as ~, and the doc-home-path guard
    row re-proved it.
    
